From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:20:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] wifi-scripts: ath12k trigger: match the ath12k_wifi7_pci
 driver

11-ath12k-trigger restarts an ath12k radio whose setup failed because
the device registered after the wireless configuration was applied. It
only acts on devices bound to the ath12k_pci driver, but since ath12k
was split into a common module and a Wi-Fi 7 one the PCI driver is
ath12k_wifi7_pci (seen on an Arista C-460 with Linux 6.18), so the
script never acts. Match both names.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
--- a/package/network/config/wifi-scripts/Makefile
+++ b/package/network/config/wifi-scripts/Makefile
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@ include $(TOPDIR)/rules.mk
 
 PKG_NAME:=wifi-scripts
 PKG_VERSION:=1.0
-PKG_RELEASE:=13
+PKG_RELEASE:=14
 PKG_LICENSE:=GPL-2.0
 
 PKG_MAINTAINER:=Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
--- a/package/network/config/wifi-scripts/files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/11-ath12k-trigger
+++ b/package/network/config/wifi-scripts/files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/11-ath12k-trigger
@@ -3,7 +3,7 @@
 # Restart ath12k radios that take long time to initialize on boot
 
 [ "${ACTION}" = "add" ] || exit 0
-[ $(grep -c DRIVER=ath12k_pci /sys/$DEVPATH/device/uevent) -gt 0 ] || exit 0
+grep -qE "^DRIVER=ath12k(_wifi7)?_pci$" /sys/$DEVPATH/device/uevent || exit 0
 
 . /usr/share/libubox/jshn.sh
 
